class: positive
summary: D1321 an array length reading `sizeof usize` or `compiler.word_size` folds at the selected target's width, so on the 32-bit models it is the same type as `[4]u8` and on a 64-bit target as `[8]u8`, whatever the host's width
program: program.ldn
constructs: 0520, 1500
targets: linux-x86-64, linux-arm64, darwin-arm64, synthetic-32, freebsd-x86-64, freebsd-arm64, linux-rv64, cortex-m0
